import Mathlib
import MassGap.MultiScaleOS

/-!
# MassGap.ApproxFromExpand — what the expansion clause gives toward `ApproxK`, and what remains

The `SU(2)` target asks
`ApproxK (kernC (CRen 2 z μ) 0) (mixKG W (CRen 2 z μ) r) (gramF W r)`. This module reads the `expand`
clause of `MultiScaleAllRen` (`CompositesRenAll.ExpandR`) against that input, proves what it gives,
and proves `ApproxK` from two clauses: the expansion in the reflection norm (`ExpandRP`) and the
generation of the flowed proxies by the observer (`ProxyGen`). No `ClayStatement` capstone is stated here:
one through `MultiScaleAllRenAt` would carry its `endpoint` field, `MultiScale.Endpoint`, which
`InputAudit.not_multiScaleEndpoint` refutes under the argued growth of the zero-flux level count.

Notation. `A_k(P) = ∏ᵢ smear a_k (cField(Pᵢ)) fᵢ` (the composite product of `P`), `B_k^s(P) =
∏ᵢ smear a_k (msProx(s, Pᵢ)) fᵢ` (the flowed proxy product at scale `s`, the observable `msLat` reads),
`Y_k(c) = ∑_Q c_Q ∏ smear a_k (Φ0 W)_k(Q)` (a real combination of the observer's margin monomials), and
`⟪X, X'⟫_k = ν_k(θX · X')`, `θ = ireflObs 0 0` (the lattice reflection form `JointRP.rform`).

## 1. What `expand` gives (proved)

* `abs_sgnC`: `|sgnC| = 1`.
* `kernC_diag_flowed`: for every separated positive-time composite monomial `P` and `η > 0`, for all
  small `s > 0`, eventually along `ultra`,
  `|sgn(P) · msLat(s)(ΘP ∪ P) − kernC(P, P)| ≤ η`. The family `ΘP ∪ P` (`pairC`, test functions of `P`
  reflected) is admissible (`CompositeLink.adm_pairC`), so `ExpandR` applies to it at its separation;
  `ConvC` (`CompositesRenAll.convC_ren_of_all`) passes the lattice reading to `contC`. So the diagonal
  term `Kc(P, P)` of `ApproxK` is the small-`s` limit of the flowed proxies' own reflected readings.

## 2. What `expand` does not give (proved on abstract kernels; argued on the real ones)

* `diag_match_not_approxK`: one composite with `Kc = 1`, one observer monomial whose Gram reading
  equals the composite's diagonal (`gForm G (single 1) (single 1) = 1 = Kc`), cross kernel `X = 0`:
  `JointRPK` holds and `ApproxK` fails. A match of the all-composite readings (here one composite, so
  only its diagonal), which is what `ExpandR` gives on reflected pairs, does not control the cross term
  `xL (X P) c`.
* ARGUED, the cross term. `ApproxK`, and the family forms `ApproxFlow.ApproxKFlow`,
  `ApproxFlow.FlowKernelConvR`, `FlowZero.UniformFlowRead`, read the mixed reading of composites
  against flowed fields in one lattice expectation. `ExpandR` quantifies over families
  `F : ι → CDatum (CRen 2 z μ)` of composites only, and compares the all-composite reading with the
  all-proxy reading `msLat`; no clause of `MultiScaleAllRen'` compares a mixed reading. In the
  reflection norm, `ExpandR` on `ΘP ∪ P` gives `⟪A, A⟫ ≈ ⟪B, B⟫` (when the proxies are reflection
  covariant, which is not stated either), not `⟪A − B, A − B⟫ → 0`.
* ARGUED, the normalisation. The family forms read the members through `Φ0 (Wf s)` on margin
  monomials with step-independent coefficients: `Φ0` scales `SymPlaqClass` fields by `a_k⁻⁴` with no
  vacuum subtraction and other fields by `1`. The proxy `msProx` carries `a_k^{−d_j}` on every index
  and the subtraction `ν_k(·)`, both step-dependent. So `B_k^s(P)` is not, at fixed coefficients, a
  combination of `Φ0 (Wf s)` margin monomials, and `ExpandR` does not reach `ApproxKFlow` for the family
  `Wf` even on its diagonal. The clauses of §3 read the proxies directly as lattice observables.

## 3. The replacement (proved)

`proxB`, `yW`, `ExpandRP`, `ProxyGen`, `rform_symm_k`, `rform_sub_yW` are stated at every `SU(N)`
(`[NeZero N]`); `approxK_of_expandRP_SU` is the `ApproxK` derivation at every `N ≥ 2`, and
`approxK_of_expandRP` is its `N = 2` instance.

* `ExpandRP b Wf c z μ`: for every `P` and `η > 0` there is a scale `0 < s ≤ b` with, eventually along
  `ultra`, `B_k^s(P)` in the half-space algebra and `⟪A_k − B_k^s, A_k − B_k^s⟫_k ≤ η`: the composite is
  its flowed proxy in the reflection norm. It reads composites and proxies only, no observer field.
* `ProxyGen W b Wf c r`: for every `P`, every `0 < s ≤ b` and `η > 0`, real coefficients `c` on the
  margin monomials of `W` with, eventually along `ultra`, `⟪B_k^s − Y_k(c), B_k^s − Y_k(c)⟫_k ≤ η`: the
  flowed proxies at scale `s` are generated by the observer's margin monomials in the reflection norm.
  Its membership clause is a range condition on `Wf s`, the analogue of `PhysRange` for `W`, which
  `MultiScaleAllRenAt` does not state.
  It reads no composite field (only the index and test function of each insertion).
* `rform_para_le`: for a symmetric bilinear form, `⟪A − Y⟫ ≤ 2⟪A − B⟫ + 2⟪B − Y⟫` when
  `⟪(A − B) − (B − Y)⟫ ≥ 0` (parallelogram identity).
* `rform_sub_yW`: `⟪A_k − Y_k(c), A_k − Y_k(c)⟫_k = rReadC − 2 xL(rMixC) c + gForm(latSF) c c`
  (`JointRP.rform_expand`).
* `approxK_of_expandRP_SU`: `ClassMoments` and `PhysRange r` of `W`, `CompOS (CRen N z μ)`, `ExpandRP` and
  `ProxyGen` give `ApproxK (kernC (CRen N z μ) 0) (mixKG W …) (gramF W r)`. The three blocks converge
  along `ultra` (`CompositesRen.reflLimG_of_cov`, `reflCovLat_CRen`, `mixConvG_of_cov`;
  `tendsto_contSF` with `ClaySUGap.uB`); the lattice value is at most `2η + 2η'` by `rform_para_le`
  and `stateK_rp` (all three products eventually in the half-space algebra:
  `JointRP.eventually_cMono_mem` with `unifLocal_buildRen`, `JointRP.eventually_flow_mem`, and the
  membership clause of `ExpandRP`).

## 4. Generation (argued; no declaration)

* `ProxyGen` is not derivable from `MultiScaleAllRen'`. Its clauses relate `Wf s` to `W` only through
  `Wf b = W`; `scale` bounds one-site moments of each `Wf s` separately and `expand` relates composites to
  proxies. Under a semigroup flow, `W = Wf b` is `Wf s` followed by the flow over `b − s`, so the fields
  of `W` are functions of the fields of `Wf s`: the inclusion runs from `W` into `Wf s`, not the one
  `ProxyGen` asks for (`s < b`). A flow at smaller time is not a function of the flow at larger time.
* `ProxyGen` is the generation statement, separated from the composites: it asks no composite reading,
  no renormalisation factor `z`, no mixing `μ`. `ExpandRP` is the short-distance statement, separated
  from the observer. `ApproxObserver.exists_jointRPK_not_approxK` shows that positivity alone does not
  give `ApproxK`; here the input that excludes a decoupled component is `ProxyGen`.
* `ProxyGen`'s `P` include monomials whose test functions sit at times `≤ r`, inside the observer's
  margin (`MarginMono` asks `r < d`); `ApproxK` asks the same of the composites (the margin reduction of `ApproxObserver.mem_of_apply_mem` is not
  built for the proxies either).
* `ExpandRP` and `ExpandR` are incomparable as stated. By Cauchy–Schwarz in the reflection form,
  `ExpandRP` gives the diagonal reflected reading `⟪A_P, A_P⟫ ≈ ⟪B_P^s, B_P^s⟫` at its chosen scale along
  `ultra`, which is the `msLat` reading only when the proxies are reflection covariant; off-diagonal pairs
  would need a scale common to `P` and `P'`, which `ExpandRP` does not supply. It gives no rate `(s/d)^ε`,
  no range `0 < s ≤ θd`, and no family that is not a reflected pair. `ExpandR` does not give `ExpandRP`
  (§2). Neither implication is built here.

Foundational footprint only (`#print axioms` at the end).

DERIVED (module-wide): `2` is `SU(2)`, the cross-term factor and the parallelogram factor; `4` the
dimension and the split of the tolerance `ε / 4`; `0` the plane, the reflection constant, the signs
and the limit; `1` the unit composite, the unit kernel and the sign's modulus; `1/2` the tolerance of
the abstract counterexample.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

noncomputable section

namespace MassGap.ApproxFromExpand

open Filter
open scoped Topology
open MassGap MassGap.InfiniteLattice MassGap.ContinuumField MassGap.ContinuumSchwinger
  MassGap.ContinuumFlow MassGap.ClayStatement MassGap.CompositeLink MassGap.JointRP
open MassGap.ExistenceReduce MassGap.NonTrivialCanonical MassGap.ClayWiring
open MassGap.ObserverOS MassGap.ObserverOSGrowth
  MassGap.ObserverOSSchwartz MassGap.ObserverOSTempered MassGap.ObserverEnergyBox
  MassGap.ObserverOSEuclidS MassGap.ObserverOSReconstructionS MassGap.ObserverOSLinked
  MassGap.ObserverRotation MassGap.ContinuumTimeGroup
  MassGap.ClayFull MassGap.ObserverNontrivial MassGap.ContinuumHypercubic
  MassGap.ObserverSymField MassGap.ObserverEnergyMoments
  MassGap.PreObserver MassGap.CompositesBuild MassGap.ObsLead MassGap.ClayData MassGap.ReflAvg
